# Two process groups orphaned at once, each with a stopped member (roadmap
# memory.md M7's review; tests/posix/orphans.c): both are hung up, though
# the first's SIGHUP ends a process within the end of the one that
# orphaned them.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_ORPHANS
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
timeout: 120
---
orphans: a session of its own: 1
orphans: the orphaned stopped job B hung up: yes
orphans: done
